msgstr "Interrogare gli input richiesti e gli output attesi {#query-the-required-inputs-and-expected-outputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The easiest way to see the required inputs and expected outputs is to print the [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") object. Array items are formatted as `'{name}' <{type}[{shape}...]>`, and the required inputs precede the optional inputs.\n"
msgstr "Il modo più semplice per vedere gli input richiesti e gli output attesi è stampare l'oggetto [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\"). Gli elementi array sono formattati come `'{name}' <{type}[{shape}...]>` e gli input richiesti precedono quelli opzionali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") and [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") of the samplex, as well as more detailed information like their names, shapes, types, and descriptions, can also be queried programatically. The return type of both of these methods is a [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"). For example, the following code lists all specifications of the input interface:\n"
msgstr "Gli [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") e gli [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") del samplex, così come informazioni più dettagliate come nomi, forme, tipi e descrizioni, possono anche essere interrogati in modo programmatico. Il tipo restituito da entrambi i metodi è un [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"). Ad esempio, il codice seguente elenca tutte le specifiche dell'interfaccia di input:\n"

